  "reasoning": "The patient presents with itchy red spots all over the body, accompanied by fever, headache, and exhaustion. This symptom cluster strongly points to chicken pox, which classically manifests as a widespread, intensely itchy rash of red spots or blisters, along with systemic viral symptoms like fever, headache, and fatigue. This aligns precisely with training reference [1], which describes 'little red spots all over my body,' exhaustion, and a severe headache, resulting in a diagnosis of chicken pox. While dengue can also cause red spots and headache, it typically features severe body/joint pain and vomiting, which are absent here. Allergy and drug reaction lack the characteristic fever and widespread vesicular rash profile. Therefore, chicken pox is the most accurate diagnosis.",
